"premodern":"not_legal","standard":"legal","standardbrawl":"legal","timeless":"legal","tlr":"legal","vintage":"legal"},"loyalty":null,"mana_cost":"","name":"Wastes","oracle_id":"05d24b0c-904a-46b6-b42a-96a4d91a0dd4","oracle_text":"{T}: Add {C}.","power":null,"produced_mana":["C"],"released_at":"2025-08-01","toughness":null,"type_line":"Basic Land"}],"fixture_kind":"public_exact-list_card_data","rulings":[{"comment":"Because Wastes is a basic land, you can include as many of them as you like in your Constructed decks.","oracle_id":"05d24b0c-904a-46b6-b42a-96a4d91a0dd4","published_at":"2021-03-19","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"In Limited events (including Sealed Deck and Booster Draft), Wastes must be in your card pool to be included in your deck. You can't add Wastes to your card pool in the same way that you can add other basic lands.","oracle_id":"05d24b0c-904a-46b6-b42a-96a4d91a0dd4","published_at":"2021-03-19","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Wastes is not a land type. If something asks you to name a land type, you can't choose Wastes.","oracle_id":"05d24b0c-904a-46b6-b42a-96a4d91a0dd4","published_at":"2021-03-19","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"A card with a splice ability can\u2019t be spliced onto itself because the spell is on the stack (and not in your hand) when you reveal the cards you want to splice onto it.","oracle_id":"3d165dec-1821-4d3f-8407-8ce8bb347f8b","published_at":"2013-06-07","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If all of the spell\u2019s targets are illegal when the spell tries to resolve, it won\u2019t resolve and none of its effects will happen.","oracle_id":"3d165dec-1821-4d3f-8407-8ce8bb347f8b","published_at":"2013-06-07","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"You choose all targets for the spell after revealing cards you want to splice, including any targets required by the text of any of those cards. You may choose a different target for each instance of the word \u201ctarget\u201d on the resulting spell.","oracle_id":"3d165dec-1821-4d3f-8407-8ce8bb347f8b","published_at":"2013-06-07","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"You reveal all cards you intend to splice at the same time. Each individual card can be spliced only once onto any one spell.","oracle_id":"3d165dec-1821-4d3f-8407-8ce8bb347f8b","published_at":"2013-06-07","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If, during a player\u2019s declare attackers step, a creature is tapped, is affected by a spell or ability that says it can\u2019t attack, or hasn\u2019t been under that player\u2019s control continuously since the turn began (and doesn\u2019t have haste), then it doesn\u2019t attack. If there\u2019s a cost associated with having a creature attack, the player isn\u2019t forced to pay that cost, so it doesn\u2019t have to attack in that case either.","oracle_id":"4a480736-4cdc-4e3a-a8cb-d1c726982f9f","published_at":"2011-09-22","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Players may still activate abilities during combat.","oracle_id":"4a480736-4cdc-4e3a-a8cb-d1c726982f9f","published_at":"2011-09-22","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"While Basandra, Battle Seraph is on the battlefield, players can\u2019t cast any spells during the combat phase, including permanent spells with flash.","oracle_id":"4a480736-4cdc-4e3a-a8cb-d1c726982f9f","published_at":"2011-09-22","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If, during a player\u2019s declare attackers step, a creature is tapped, is affected by a spell or ability that says it can\u2019t attack, or hasn\u2019t been under that player\u2019s control continuously since the turn began (and doesn\u2019t have haste), then it doesn\u2019t attack. If there\u2019s a cost associated with having a creature attack, the player isn\u2019t forced to pay that cost, so it doesn\u2019t have to attack in that case either.","oracle_id":"4b8fb8dc-f1c5-4994-8a58-4849e7e85539","published_at":"2011-01-22","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"The creature\u2019s controller still decides which player or planeswalker the creature attacks.","oracle_id":"4b8fb8dc-f1c5-4994-8a58-4849e7e85539","published_at":"2011-01-22","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If a token is exiled this way, it will cease to exist and won't return to the battlefield.","oracle_id":"6879f5ce-7a1b-4606-bad1-885779b0d456","published_at":"2018-03-16","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Once the exiled permanent returns, it's considered a new object with no relation to the object that it was. Auras attached to the exiled permanent will be put into their owners' graveyards. Equipment attached to the exiled permanent will become unattached and remain on the battlefield. Any counters on the exiled permanent will cease to exist.","oracle_id":"6879f5ce-7a1b-4606-bad1-885779b0d456","published_at":"2018-03-16","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"The returned card won't be the target of any spells or abilities that targeted it before. Any spells that don't target, such as Akroma's Vengeance, will still affect it.","oracle_id":"6879f5ce-7a1b-4606-bad1-885779b0d456","published_at":"2018-03-16","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"When an effect returns the exiled card \"under your control,\" you control it indefinitely after that. In a multiplayer game, if a player leaves the game, all cards that player owns leave as well. If you leave the game, any creatures you control from Cloudshift's effect are exiled.","oracle_id":"6879f5ce-7a1b-4606-bad1-885779b0d456","published_at":"2018-03-16","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If an attacking creature loses haste, perhaps because Fervor leaves the battlefield after attackers have been declared, it won't be removed from combat.","oracle_id":"8e0cea9c-3110-4728-9378-76849e33bb90","published_at":"2012-07-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If, during its controller\u2019s declare attackers step, a creature affected by Rage Nimbus\u2019s activated ability is tapped, is affected by a spell or ability that says it can\u2019t attack, or is affected by \u201csummoning sickness,\u201d then that creature doesn\u2019t attack. If there\u2019s a cost associated with having that creature attack, its controller isn\u2019t forced to pay that cost, so the creature doesn\u2019t have to attack in that case either.","oracle_id":"ab5b49d4-e648-43f1-bcc0-7dd4763316ee","published_at":"2010-06-15","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"A creature that attacks each turn if able must attack only once that turn. It is not forced into each attack that turn. However, a creature that attacks each combat if able must attack again if it can.","oracle_id":"dc1c0e8c-d0c1-445c-968f-7dec91e5d5fc","published_at":"2025-09-19","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Abilities that trigger when a creature attacks, blocks, or is blocked will trigger during each combat that turn.","oracle_id":"dc1c0e8c-d0c1-445c-968f-7dec91e5d5fc","published_at":"2025-09-19","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If you manage to cast this during a main phase of your opponent's turn, that opponent's creatures will untap and that opponent will be able to attack again. It will not allow you to attack during their turn.","oracle_id":"dc1c0e8c-d0c1-445c-968f-7dec91e5d5fc","published_at":"2025-09-19","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Relentless Assault creates an additional combat and main phase only if it resolves during a main phase.","oracle_id":"dc1c0e8c-d0c1-445c-968f-7dec91e5d5fc","published_at":"2025-09-19","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"In the Two-Headed Giant format, you still only have to pay once per creature.","oracle_id":"e828b189-0e8f-43b8-b909-4c23e742e028","published_at":"2007-02-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Unless some effect explicitly says otherwise, a creature that can't attack you can still attack a planeswalker you control.","oracle_id":"e828b189-0e8f-43b8-b909-4c23e742e028","published_at":"2014-02-01","source":"wotc"}],"schema_version":1,"source":"Scryfall Oracle/rulings subset for offline tests"}
